    "summary": "Fiery 'Friend of Mine' and monster Dark Star with tight jams",
    "blurb": "The May 31, 1969 Oregon show delivers a soaring rendition of He Was A Friend Of Mine, a monster Dark Star, and an inspired Baby Blue finale. Jerry’s guitar shines while the band rides high‑octane segues from The Other One into Cryptical Envelopment. Overall a high‑energy performance captured on solid soundboard sources.",
    "review": "The May 31, 1969 concert at McArthur Court finds the Dead firing on all cylinders. Early in Set 1 they weave through bluesy rock with a crisp Hard To Handle and a heartfelt Green Green Grass Of Home before launching into the classic “Cryptical Envelopment → The Other One → Cryptical Envelopment” sandwich that feels both tight and exploratory. Set 2 kicks off with an epic He Was A Friend Of Mine, where Jerry’s tone is on fire, then bursts into a monster Dark Star that rides the full spectrum of psychedelic intensity. Though Doin’ That Rag suffers a brief cut, the band quickly recovers for Cosmic Charlie and closes the night with a beautifully rendered It’s All Over Now Baby Blue, showcasing Bob’s warm vocal delivery. The soundboard recordings capture this high‑energy set with enough clarity to hear every nuance, making it one of the standout late‑60s shows.",
